WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:06.490
In 1958, two scientists grew bacteria
on heavy nitrogen for many generations,

2
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.000
until all their DNA was heavy.

3
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.850
Then they moved the bacteria
to normal, light nitrogen.

4
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.160
Every new strand made
after that was light.

5
00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:20.250
Spun hard in a tube,
DNA settles by density.

6
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.730
Heavier DNA settles lower.

7
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:27.600
So how could one experiment show that
every new DNA molecule keeps half of the

8
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:28.830
old one?

9
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.470
In this mission, you'll meet
three rival models of copying,

10
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.840
each making a different prediction.

11
00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:38.430
Then you'll read the bands,
generation by generation,

12
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.730
and see which models survive.

13
00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:45.700
Your mission: find out how one experiment
with heavy nitrogen showed what each

14
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.730
new DNA molecule keeps.
